 ## Background
-The method originates from the need to improve the visual quality of volume rendering by reducing artifacts caused by regular sampling patterns [S1, unofficial]. The specific formula using sine and fractional part extraction is a common technique in computer graphics for generating pseudo-random numbers from spatial coordinates [G]. It is widely used in real-time rendering engines and shaders [G].
+The technique is commonly used in volumetric ray casting to improve the visual quality of rendered volumes by breaking up regular sampling patterns [S1, unofficial]. It is a simple yet effective method for reducing aliasing and banding artifacts.
 
